{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Mixpanel adapter for Swidux’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":". Owns the Mixpanel SDK on the app’s behalf — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelAnalyticsService(token:)"},{"type":"text","text":" calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Mixpanel.initialize"},{"type":"text","text":" internally so apps never need to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Mixpanel"},{"type":"text","text":". Ships a recording mock for previews and tests."}],"metadata":{"role":"collection","title":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","externalID":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics"}],"roleHeading":"Framework"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the bridge between Mixpanel’s iOS SDK and Swidux’s provider-agnostic analytics plugin. The plugin owns analytics state (opt-out flag, current screen, last-identified user) and converts your domain actions into typed ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsEvent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" values; this package translates those events into Mixpanel SDK calls and maps ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsValue","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" into Mixpanel’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Properties","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" payload.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Two types ship in a single product:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":" — the live "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":" conformer that constructs and wraps a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelInstance"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MockMixpanelAnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":" — a recording actor for SwiftUI "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#Preview"},{"type":"text","text":" blocks and Swift Testing suites."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The flow:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["store.send(.counter(.increment(5)))","  → AnalyticsPlugin runs the mapper in afterReduce","  → mapper emits AnalyticsEvent(\"counter_added\", [\"amount\": .int(5)])","  → MixpanelAnalyticsService.track(_:) forwards to MixpanelInstance.track(event:properties:)","  → Mixpanel SDK queues the event and flushes per its own schedule"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin and the adapter stay decoupled: the plugin doesn’t know about Mixpanel, and the adapter doesn’t know about your action tree.","type":"text"}]}]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Quickstart","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/GettingStarted"],"anchor":"Quickstart"},{"title":"How-to Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/HowToImplementService","doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/HowToPreviewAndTest"],"anchor":"How-to-Guides"},{"title":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/ServiceReference","doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MockServiceReference"],"anchor":"Reference"},{"title":"Explanation","iden